<title>FRANCE: Lafarge buys Laporte Italian units.</title>
<headline>Lafarge buys Laporte Italian units.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lafarge Peintures has recently bought Italy's Settef and Chamberlain from Laporte Plc of Britain, parent company Lafarge of France said on Friday.</p>
<p>Settef has annual turnover of 60 million francs and specialises in decorative wall coverings for interiors and exteriors. Chamberlain has annual revenues of 50 million francs and specialises in organic glues, particularly for flexible floor coverings.</p>
<p>No prices were given for the deals. Lafarge specialises in cement and building materials.</p>
</text>
